# Supabase connection. Both values are PUBLIC by design (they ship inside the app; Row Level Security protects data).
# Find them in Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys (URL: Project Settings -> Data API).
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL       Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  Publishable key (sb_publishable_...) or the legacy "anon" key
# NEVER put the Secret key or the legacy service_role key in any env file, the app or GitHub.
#
# Production build (GitHub Pages): the values live in .env.production, which is committed; the deploy workflow
# checks it with scripts/check-public-config.mjs.
# Local development: copy this file to .env and fill it in. Leave both empty to run in "Mode Demo"
# (data stored only in this browser). Only VITE_ variables belong here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
